WEBVTT

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.950
Only five people have been called here today.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.770
And only one will be selected from these five.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:12.050
This may be harsh, but it's the reality of the world of professional motorsports.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.920
We want a driver who can win.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.730
One who can answer his team's requests and bring out the most from the machines...

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.430
This is to find a winning driver.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:29.310
All of you, who have come this far,
 should know that by now.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:36.620
In this final selection,
 please convince us that you have what it takes.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.000
We're looking forward to it.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.400
Yes.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:50.790
<i>I'll show them all who the fastest is!</i>

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.930
The final selection will be decided by a time attack.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:41.930
We'll have Ishihara as your pacesetter, same as at the school.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.670
You'll get two sessions in the morning, as well as in the afternoon,

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.900
for a total of four sessions.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:51.310
In the last session, we'll have you attack on new tires.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.410
Whether you produce a result or not,
 it all depends on you.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.950
After finishing all sessions,

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:01.720
each of you will be interviewed one at a time, and we will decide who gets the scholarship.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.580
Literally, this is the final battle.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.840
Do your best.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.340
That is all.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:08.800
Yes!

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.210
Huh?

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.680
Don't you want to go to the pits, Nobu-kun?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.440
No, it's okay.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.690
I'll stay here.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:27.650
There's nothing I can do for him now, anyway.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:29.380
That's true.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.830
It's not like before anymore.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.580
Coming this far on your first challenge...

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.230
You're amazing, Monami.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.500
You don't have to worry about the results—

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.250
I'll win.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:52.590
This is a match, so it won't be any good unless you believe you can win, right?

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.610
Same goes for you, Ca-chan.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.470
Believe that you can win.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:00.060
Good luck.

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:31.880
Everything is ready at the starting line!

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.010
So, how much practice has each of them had prior to this?

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.100
Let's see...

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:39.000
They've all practiced quite a bit.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:45.520
Especially Shiba in car #2, who borrowed a car from Liarize and practiced a fair bit.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:50.150
It's only Taira in #1 who hasn't practiced at all.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.070
Yeah, he does look like he doesn't have money.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:56.240
On the spot as always, huh?

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.880
It's finally here.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:04.230
Start with a bang and impress them, Capeta.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:05.810
That's impossible, Uncle.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.290
Huh?  Is it?

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:08.350
Yeah.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:14.750
It's his first time on this course, and the aim is to get used to it on secondhand tires.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.510
He has to find his best line during the sessions.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:23.430
Then he goes for the time attack on new tires.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:25.940
That's when the match is decided.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.160
I see.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.880
<i>Nobu.  Monami.</i>

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:49.140
<i>I'll get a result no matter what!</i>

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.090
<i>Taira.</i>

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:57.090
<i>I'll beat you this time and show everyone!</i>

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.440
<b>Ishihara, start!</b>

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.650
<b>Next.  Taira, start!</b>

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.320
They've started!

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.940
It's the start of the first session.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:19.300
So, that car #1 is Capeta.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.670
<b>Shiba, start!</b>

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:52.280
<i>Oh, God...  What's with this huge course?!</i>

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.230
<i>It's completely different from the school's course.</i>

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:06.450
<i>It's long!</i>

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:11.420
<i>I can't see ahead, and while I'd like to step harder on the accelerator...</i>

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:14.880
<i>the rear is slowly being dragged to the outside!</i>

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:18.550
<i>I don't want any losses here!</i>

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:25.570
<i>Damn!</i>

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.470
<i>Now it's a steep hill.</i>

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:30.020
<i>I'm suddenly stalling!</i>

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:37.590
<i>It's long...</i>

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.650
<i>I can't see ahead!</i>

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:42.600
<i>How am I supposed to get a time out of this?!</i>

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.040
<i>Damn!</i>

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.540
<i>But this is fun!</i>

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.340
All right, it's started!

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.590
Go, Capeta!

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.200
<i>That Taira...</i>

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:10.180
<i>Looks like he's still trying to find his line.</i>

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:11.600
<i>This is my chance.</i>

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.450
<i>I'll show him the difference!</i>

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.620
<i>Don't get hasty, Ryou.</i>

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:22.780
<i>You've had plenty of practice, unlike Taira.</i>

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:33.330
How is it, Nobu-kun?

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:35.290
Yeah.  I think he's okay.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:54.350
Why did I have to wake up early today and come watch this?

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:00.200
We're going to take one of these drivers into our works team no matter what.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:04.110
Isn't it best to see the driving of next year's rival?

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.220
It doesn't concern me.

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:11.630
Like I'm going to lose to a slacker from the school.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:13.480
Just you watch!

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:38.670
<b>1st session finished!</b>

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:39.810
<b>All cars pit in!</b>

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:00.670
<i>Shiba got 48.2 seconds?!</i>

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:03.790
<i>He's already 2 seconds faster than me?!</i>

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:07.510
<i>He's practiced a lot.</i>

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:13.800
He's in 5th place, huh?

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.020
This is tough.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.290
Nobu-kun.

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:20.020
Is it true that the last two cars don't get new tires later on?

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:25.500
It's because there's no point investing in slow drivers.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.990
So the last two drivers in the final session should assume they're finished.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:32.090
That's how it is in the world of motor racing.

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.990
I wonder if he'll be okay.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:35.560
He'll be okay.

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:36.700
This is Capeta.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.030
He'll do it.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.420
I believe in him.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:51.640
<i>It doesn't matter if you've practiced or not.</i>

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:57.020
<i>The point is, I have to get the top time like I did at the school.</i>

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:03.580
<i>I don't want to lose.</i>

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:06.130
<i>I won't lose to him!</i>

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.300
Taira, huh?

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:31.260
They said he crashed during the mock race.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:35.260
And his driving is still wild and rough.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:40.440
But there's something that heats up the people watching him.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:41.230
Right?

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:47.400
Do you know about the legendary race in the rain at Haruna?

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:50.400
Amidst the cars going off course due to the sudden rain...

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:55.530
<b>2nd session finished!</b>

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.990
<i>There's still a 1.4-second gap.</i>

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.350
You've got the new tires.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:07.900
You should be happy, Taira.

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:08.630
Yes...

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.580
<i>As expected, Taira is coming.</i>

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:17.810
<i>I don't want to lose!</i>

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:23.230
Where did you go, Shin-chan?

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:26.630
Were you that curious about Taira's driving on the 5th corner?

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:27.600
No.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.220
We can look forward to the afternoon sessions.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.820
Something might happen.

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:31.940
"Come."

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.650
"Come out, star of tomorrow!"

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:35.460
That sort of feeling.

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:41.490
Nobu-kun, aren't you eating?

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.290
I'll eat as soon as I finish this.

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:55.960
<i>You're doing it, Ca-chan!</i>

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.200
<i>All right.</i>

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:15.280
Could you get the standby ready?

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:30.740
<i>Just as I thought.</i>

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:31.960
<i>This is much faster.</i>

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:48.190
<i>Shiba's driving is textbook beautiful.</i>

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:54.190
<i>Taira is also turning the corners without killing his speed.</i>

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:56.690
<i>His senses are really good...</i>

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.200
<i>Surely this is a buy!</i>

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:05.400
It's an awkward feeling.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:12.340
If he passes this, I won't be able to see that great overtake again on the kart!

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:15.630
<i>Kart maker Harada-san.</i>

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:17.950
<i>Why is he here?</i>

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:23.770
Hello.

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:27.650
Capeta-kun's chase is spectacular as always.

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:29.900
We can't relax our attention for a second.

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:31.260
Not at all.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:34.360
Shiba-kun's time is also great.

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:40.200
Well, we've had plenty of practice,
having borrowed a machine from Liarize, you see.

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:43.660
<i>He got us.</i>

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:48.040
W-Well, I wish you all the best.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.380
Nobu-kun, isn't that...

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.970
<i>He practiced on a machine from Liarize?!</i>

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:57.340
<i>This may be big.</i>

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:03.010
What's going on, Nobu?!

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:05.140
You haven't contacted me since then!

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:08.440
<b>Numbers 11 to 15.</b>

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:10.660
<b>Please make your way to the side of the stage.</b>

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:12.100
Damn!

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:14.730
I'm not gonna let you off for this!

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:17.320
Nobu-kun.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:22.440
I have this feeling that there isn't much of a gap between Shiba-kun and Capeta.

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:38.180
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:39.700
<i>It won't grip the road surface.</i>

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:41.470
<i>It should be the same for Taira!</i>

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:53.260
<i>I keep drifting outside!</i>

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:54.560
<i>I can't mess up!</i>

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:06.460
<b>3rd session, finished!</b>

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:14.460
Capeta's time isn't getting shorter.

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:18.260
I bet his tires were wearing out.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.920
It's the same with Shiba.

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:25.510
In either case, I didn't think everyone would have practiced so much.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.770
That doesn't matter.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:31.830
He suddenly started driving and he was fast.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:34.440
I believe in Capeta's adaptability.

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:37.980
It's okay.

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:41.950
He'll give us a result in the final session with new tires.

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:43.800
I believe in him.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:45.410
I believe in him 100%!

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:49.240
Like he believed in me.

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:06.970
<i>Monami.  Nobu.</i>

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:08.430
<i>I'll...</i>

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:11.930
<i>win no matter what!</i>

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.320
#14, Suzuki Monami.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.230
The final session.

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:43.550
Laugh or cry, this is the last chance!

00:17:44.490 --> 00:17:45.590
Capeta.

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:53.890
<i>What a grip!</i>

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:56.400
<i>I can win with this!</i>

